# Aristo runtime artifacts produced by dogfooding the SDK on its own source.
# `aristo.toml` and `.aristo/` are BOTH tracked — they carry project state
# (config decisions, the stamped annotation index, verify specs, generated
# docs) that needs to propagate to CI and fresh clones. The pre-commit
# hook runs `aristo stamp` before every commit, so `.aristo/index.toml`
# stays in sync with source at commit time. Downstream Aristo users
# commit these artifacts too (per docs/TOOLS.md "Committed to the repo
# by default") — this repo dogfoods that same convention.
/.github/workflows/aristo.yml
